title: A Red Town Hall
subtitle: The party wins a town council.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('red_town'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('red_town');
RG.news('Communists the largest party on the town council of ' + Q.lw_town, 2);
RG.ledger('The party won the town council of ' + Q.lw_town + '.', 'lw_redtown_' + Q.lw_town);
!}

= A Red Town Hall

In the municipal elections in **[+ lw_town +]**, the communist list has come first. With a vote or two from the left, the party can elect the mayor and run the town: its schools, its gasworks, its housing office and its police, as far as the government of [+ lw_land +] allows. None of the comrades has run anything bigger than a union branch.

- @govern: Govern for the workers: rents, school meals, coal.
- @fortress: Swear in the red guard as the town police.
- @tribune: Refuse the mayoralty.

@govern
subtitle: Practical work that wins members. Some will call it municipal reformism.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.1, loyalty: 4});
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
!}

The council freezes the rents in the town's flats and opens the school kitchens to every child. Workers from the next town come to see how it is done.

@fortress
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The town's police and its arms for the red guard. The state will send troops.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('uprising');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {guards: 1.5, militancy: 5, repression: 15});
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
RG.news('Red guard takes over the municipal police in ' + Q.lw_town, 2);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 6);
!}

The new mayor swears in a hundred men of the red guard as auxiliary police. Within a month the government sends a commissioner, and within two it sends troops.

@tribune
subtitle: Clean hands, and a social democratic mayor.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 3, members: -0.02});
if (Q.ultraleft_gone) { RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 3); } else { RG.lw.lean('ultraleft', 1, 4); }
!}

The party's councillors use every session to denounce the system. The sessions are well attended.
